Here's a sample End User API for 3D Camera Animation in TypeScript:

```typescript
import { Camera, Scene } from 'three';

class ThreeCameraAnimationAPI {
  private scene: Scene;
  private camera: Camera;

  constructor(scene: Scene, camera: Camera) {
    this.scene = scene;
    this.camera = camera;
  }

  public animate() {
    requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());
    this.update();
    this.render();
  }

  public update() {
    // Update camera position and rotation
    this.camera.position.x += 0.1;
    this.camera.rotation.y += 0.1;
  }

  public render() {
    this.scene.render();
  }
}

const scene = new Scene();
const camera = new Camera();
camera.position.set(0, 0, 5);
camera.lookAt(scene.position);

const api = new ThreeCameraAnimationAPI(scene, camera);
api.animate();
```

This API provides basic camera animation functionality, including updating the camera position and rotation, and rendering the scene. You can customize the animation logic by modifying the `update` method.

To use this API, you'll need to include the Three.js library in your project and create a new instance of the `ThreeCameraAnimationAPI` class with your scene and camera objects. Then, call the `animate` method to start the animation.

