```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    if (words[i].match(/^(\w+)\s+(\w+)$/)) {
      adjectives.push(words[i]);
    }
  }

  if (adjectives.length > 1) {
    const firstAdjective = adjectives.shift();
    const lastAdjective = adjectives.pop();

    adjectives.unshift(lastAdjective);
    adjectives.push(firstAdjective);

    return adjectives.join(" ");
  } else {
    return sentence;
  }
}

const sentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const result = switchAdjectives(sentence);
console.log(result); // Output: Green beautiful trees are in the park
```

This function splits the input sentence into an array of words, then filters out the adjectives using a regular expression. If there are multiple adjectives, it swaps the first and last adjectives in the array, then joins the array back into a sentence. If there are no adjectives, it returns the original sentence.

