```javascript
function smoothLinearMap(x) {
  const smoothingFactor = 0.5; // Adjust this value to control the smoothness
  const linearRangeStart = 0.3; // Adjust this value to control the linear range start point
  const linearRangeEnd = 0.7; // Adjust this value to control the linear range end point

  if (x <= linearRangeStart) {
    return x * x; // Smooth start
  } else if (x >= linearRangeEnd) {
    return 1 - (1 - x) * x; // Smooth stop
  } else {
    return x; // Linear range
  }
}
```

This function uses a simple square function for the smooth start and stop parts, and a linear function for the linear range. The `smoothingFactor` controls the smoothness of the transition between the different parts of the function. You can adjust this value to your liking.

The `linearRangeStart` and `linearRangeEnd` values control the range over which the linear part of the function applies. You can adjust these values to control the width of the linear range.

