            $table->id();
            $table->string('name');
            $table->email('email');
            $table->password('password');
            $table->timestamps();

            // Relationships
            $table->hasMany('cars');
            $table->hasMany('pets');
            $table->hasOne('house');
        });
    }

    /**
     * Reverse the migrations.
     *
     * @return void
     */
    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('users');
    }
}
```

This migration creates a `users` table with an `id`, `name`, `email`, `password`, and `timestamps`. It also defines relationships for the user model to have many `cars`, `pets`, and `houses`. The `house` relationship is of type `hasOne`, meaning that each user can only have one house.

