4. Add the object to the organized data array.
5. Return the organized data array.

Here's the code to accomplish this in JavaScript:
```javascript
function organizeWordsByLength(words) {
  const organizedData = [];

  for (const word of words) {
    const length = word.length;
    const obj = { word, length };
    organizedData.push(obj);
